  "query_preview": "the high surf advisory for Kosrae until 3 PM Tuesday. If\nthose winds keep up, it may need to be extended further.\n\nWestern Micronesia...\nConvection associated with the NET has drifted south of Palau, Yap\nand Chuuk, resulting in a dry forecast for the next several days at\nPalau and Yap, and through midweek for Chuuk. Palau and Yap can\nexpect only spotty light to isolated showers into the the weekend.\nFor Chuuk, isolated showers will continue through Wednesday.\nWednesday night, a weak trade-wind trough looks to move through \nChuuk, bringing an increase in showers to Weno, with a drier pattern\nback by Thursday morning. Over the weekend, the NET is expected to \nbecome a bit more active, resulting in another round of increased \nshowers.\n\nBenign marine conditions will continue across the region, with seas\nmostly between 4 and 6 feet through the period. Gentle to moderate\nwinds will become light to gentle the last half of the week.",
